{"name":"Deck Crew","hex":"#5e7cac","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"deck","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any raised flat surface that can be walked on: a balcony; a porch; a raised patio; a flat rooftop.","The floorlike covering of the horizontal sections, or compartments, of a ship or boat. Small vessels have only one deck; larger ships have two or three decks."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To furnish with a deck.","To knock (someone) to the floor, especially with a single punch."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/deck"},{"term":"crew","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A group of people together\n Any company of people; an assemblage; a throng.\n\nA group of people (often staff) manning and operating a large facility or piece of equipment such as a factory, ship, boat, airplane, or spacecraft.","Any company of people; an assemblage; a throng."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To be a member of a vessel's crew.","To be a member of a work or production crew."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/crew"}],"entries":[{"title":"Crew","blocks":[{"text":"A crew is a body or a group of people who work at a common activity, generally in a structured or hierarchical organization. A location in which a crew works is called a crewyard or a workyard. The word has nautical resonances: the tasks involved in operating a ship, particularly a sailing ship, providing numerous specialities within a ship's crew, often organised with a chain of command. Traditional nautical usage strongly distinguishes officers from crew, though the two groups combined form the ship's company. Members of a crew are often referred to by the titles crewmate, crewman or crew-member."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/72/STS-112_crew.jpg/330px-STS-112_crew.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crew","wikidata":"Q345844"}],"images":[],"sounds":{"deck":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/c/ca/En-us-deck.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/c/ca/En-us-deck.ogg/En-us-deck.ogg.mp3"}],"crew":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/8/8d/En-us-crew.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/8/8d/En-us-crew.ogg/En-us-crew.ogg.mp3"}]},"pictures":[{"title":"USS Kearsarge (CVS-33) crew spells out 'Mercury 9' on the flight deck on 15 May 1963 (GPN-2000-001403)","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/USS_Kearsarge_%28CVS-33%29_crew_spells_out_%27Mercury_9%27_on_the_flight_deck_on_15_May_1963_%28GPN-2000-001403%29.jpg/500px-USS_Kearsarge_%28CVS-33%29_crew_spells_out_%27Mercury_9%27_on_the_flight_deck_on_15_May_1963_%28GPN-2000-001403%29.jpg","ratio":1.288659793814433,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:USS_Kearsarge_(CVS-33)_crew_spells_out_%27Mercury_9%27_on_the_flight_deck_on_15_May_1963_(GPN-2000-001403).jpg","share":0.215},{"title":"20131003 Schoeningen Palaeon DSC08394 PtrQs","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/20131003_Schoeningen_Palaeon_DSC08394_PtrQs.jpg/500px-20131003_Schoeningen_Palaeon_DSC08394_PtrQs.jpg","ratio":1.5,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:20131003_Schoeningen_Palaeon_DSC08394_PtrQs.jpg","share":0.2075},{"title":"2018 01 (Blue) - Chaouen","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/2018_01_%28Blue%29_-_Chaouen.jpg/500px-2018_01_%28Blue%29_-_Chaouen.jpg","ratio":1.5,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:2018_01_(Blue)_-_Chaouen.jpg","share":0.17375},{"title":"Lake Geneva from Chillon Castle","image":"https://thumb.wikim